{"name":"Aquatic","hex":"#99c1cc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aquatic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to water; living in or near water, taking place in water."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any aquatic plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquatic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aquatic animal","blocks":[{"text":"An aquatic animal is any animal, whether vertebrate or invertebrate, that lives in a body of water for all or most of its lifetime. Aquatic animals generally conduct aquatic respiration by extracting dissolved oxygen in water via specialised respiratory organs called gills, through the skin or across enteral mucosae, although some are secondarily aquatic animals evolved from terrestrial ancestors that re-adapted to aquatic environments, in which case they actually use lungs to breathe air and are essentially holding their breath when living in water. Some species of gastropod mollusc, such as the eastern emerald sea slug, are even capable of kleptoplastic photosynthesis via endosymbiosis with ingested yellow-green algae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Jordania_zonope.jpg/330px-Jordania_zonope.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquatic_animal"},{"title":"Aquatic ecosystem","blocks":[{"text":"An aquatic ecosystem is an ecosystem found in and around a body of water, in contrast to land-based terrestrial ecosystems. Aquatic ecosystems contain communities of organisms—aquatic life—that are dependent on each other and on their environment. The two main types of aquatic ecosystems are marine ecosystems and freshwater ecosystems. Freshwater ecosystems may be lentic ; lotic ; and wetlands."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquatic_ecosystem"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg/500px-Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg/1280px-Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg/500px-Mother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sperm whales, an example of air-breathing aquatic animals","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMother_and_baby_sperm_whale.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg/500px-Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg/500px-Neuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The four main types of aquatic animals: neustons, planktons, nektons and benthos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANeuston%2C_Plankton%2C_Nekton%2C_Benthos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Maldivesfish2.jpg/500px-Maldivesfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Maldivesfish2.jpg/1280px-Maldivesfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Maldivesfish2.jpg/500px-Maldivesfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coral reefs form complex marine ecosystems with tremendous biodiversity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaldivesfish2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Panorama_presa_las_ni%C3%B1as_mogan_gran_canaria.jpg/500px-Panorama_presa_las_ni%C3%B1as_mogan_gran_canaria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Panorama_presa_las_ni%C3%B1as_mogan_gran_canaria.jpg/500px-Panorama_presa_las_ni%C3%B1as_mogan_gran_canaria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Freshwater ecosystem","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanorama_presa_las_ni%C3%B1as_mogan_gran_canaria.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg/500px-Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg/1280px-Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg/500px-Stream_in_the_redwoods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This stream operating together with its environment can be thought of as forming a river ecosystem.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStream_in_the_redwoods.jpg"}],"sounds":{"aquatic":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/En-us-aquatic.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/29/En-us-aquatic.ogg/En-us-aquatic.ogg.mp3"}]}}}